From: Constellation maintainers
Subject: [local correctness backport] Initialize the IPv4 connection lookup application
Upstream-base: 4247e24561a9cd225db73a7cfaf5c7b2c99ba0a5
Recorded: 2026-10-17

conn4_match compares application but dp_ctrl_connect_report did not assign it.
Initialize the complete key and use the report's actual Application. This
preserves the existing tuple, counters, timestamp/action and batch semantics;
it prevents undefined stack contents from splitting identical application rows.
The lookup occurs before IPC export, so a downstream Go correction cannot
repair its aggregation. Actual reporter regression: tests/native-policy/connect_report.c.
Not an upstream merge claim or an explanation of the separate Protect probe gap.

--- a/dp/ctrl.c
+++ b/dp/ctrl.c
@@ -2651,7 +2651,7 @@
 
     // TODO: Only care IPv4 sessions
     if (likely(log->EtherType == ETH_P_IP)) {
-        conn4_key_t key;
+        conn4_key_t key = {0};
 
         DEBUG_LOGGER(DBG_MAC_FORMAT" "DBG_IPV4_FORMAT":%u => "DBG_IPV4_FORMAT":%u"
                      " app=%u policy=%u action=%d sess=%d violate=%d threat=%u severity=%d\n",
@@ -2692,6 +2692,7 @@
             key.ingress = false;
         }
         key.port = log->ServerPort;
+        key.application = log->Application;
         key.ipproto = log->IPProto;
         key.pol_id = log->PolicyId;
 
